Web source: web/src/api/hooks/useFSM.ts (2 reads, 0 mutations)

Reads / queries (2/2 ported):
  [x] useFSMStats        -> FsmStore.stats / FsmRepository.stats
                            GET /fsm/stats?vehicle_id={entityId}
                            snake_case vehicle_id (matches web template literal);
                            queryKey fsmKeys.stats(entityId) -> cache key "stats:{entityId}"
                            in CacheDomain.Fsm; enabled:!!entityId gate lives in
                            FsmStore (null/blank id -> stable Loading feed, repo
                            never touched).
  [x] useFSMTransitions  -> FsmStore.transitions / FsmRepository.transitions
                            GET /fsm/transitions?vehicle_id&hours&page&per_page
                               [&fsm_name][&start&end]
                            queryKey fsmKeys.transitions(entityId, fsmType, hours,
                            page, perPage, start??'', end??'') -> per-(filter,
                            window,page) cache key via fsmTransitionsKey; same
                            enabled:!!entityId gate.

Mutations / actions (0/0):
  (none — useFSM.ts declares only two useQuery; no invalidation surface)

Derivations (pure, golden-locked, KMP+C# parity, ADR-004):
  - fsmNameParam(FsmType)         : web `fsmType === 'all' ? '' : '&fsm_name=' + fsmType`
                                    — ALL suppresses fsm_name (null); else wire value.
                                    (FsmDerivationGoldenTest.NAME_GOLDEN — 3 rows:
                                     all, vehicle, telemetry_connection)
  - buildFsmTransitionsQuery(...) : web template-literal order vehicle_id, hours,
                                    page, per_page, then conditional fsm_name, then
                                    half-open start/end ONLY when BOTH ends supplied
                                    (web `startInstant && endInstantExclusive` guard
                                    — a calendar-day-only / single-ended window never
                                    reaches the wire, which is what stops a non-UTC
                                    user from silently dropping today's local rows).
                                    (FsmDerivationGoldenTest.QUERY_GOLDEN — 5 rows:
                                     all_no_window, non_all_filter, window_both_ends,
                                     window_start_only, window_end_only; param order
                                     asserted as part of the contract)
  - fsmTransitionsKey(...)        : mirrors web fsmKeys.transitions tuple
                                    [entityId, fsmType, hours, page, perPage,
                                     start??'', end??''] for independent caching.

Caching: CacheDomain.Fsm ("fsm", 10.seconds = web INTERVALS.FAST refetch cadence);
reads emit cache->network (Resource.Loading -> Resource.Success, ADR-013). The web
hooks declare no staleTime and poll on INTERVALS.FAST; the 10s domain window keeps
the freshness flag honest while the finer refetch cadence stays a UI concern. SI
preserved verbatim (raw JsonElement; payload is not unit-bearing).

Tests: FsmRepositoryContractTest (endpoint/method/param + double-prefix-free path
+ per-key cache locks), FsmStoreTest (cache->network, enabled:!!entityId gate,
feed sharing per param tuple, scoped refresh, no-op refresh for disabled/unobserved),
FsmDerivationGoldenTest (name + query golden vectors).
